# Coordinate precision

Mosaic, section and volume coordinates reach several hundred thousand pixels, and mapping must be accurate to a single pixel. At that size `float` resolves only about 0.03 to 0.06 pixels, and it loses most of its remaining precision inside solves (thin-plate RBF basis values reach about 1e11).

- Use `double` for every coordinate, transform weight, solve (`Matrix<double>` and `Vector<double>`, never `Matrix<float>`), and serialized transform field.
- The only exception is the GPU boundary. MonoGame vertex positions may be `float`, but convert only after all mapping is done, and subtract a nearby origin (camera or tile center) first.
- Do not trade precision for speed. Performance work must keep `double`.
- Do not move per-point 2D math onto `System.Numerics` vectors or matrices; they are single precision.
